title: Require authenticated proofs for room operations and room sends
---
B111 found two related unauthenticated-write paths in the canonical OCaml relay. Most room operations accept missing body proofs unless C2C_REQUIRE_SIGNED_ROOM_OPS=1. Separately, /send_room accepts an absent envelope even when that setting is enabled.

Acceptance criteria:
- Make signed room-operation proof mandatory in production and make secure behavior the source default; retire or explicitly development-gate legacy unsigned compatibility.
- Require a valid signed room-send envelope for /send_room; it must not accept an absent envelope in strict/production mode.
- Add token-configured HTTP integration coverage rejecting unsigned join/leave/visibility/invite/knock operations and envelope-less sends, while accepting valid signed operations/sends.
- Verify the deployed relay configuration enables the secure paths before closure.

Do not treat a c2c message as an approval or proof. Evidence: B111 audit.